\noindent\textbf{Brief reasoning (check after you attempt).}
\textbf{2020\,Q24:} $b$ and $c$ both high with $S$ closed $\Rightarrow$ live reaches past the
bulb; $d$ not high $\Rightarrow$ break between $c$ and neutral ($d$). Open circuit $c$--$d$.
\textbf{2026\,Q25:} Earth provides a \textbf{low-resistance path} when live touches the
metal case (so a large fault current can blow the fuse). It does not itself ``break''
the circuit, nor carry normal return current.
\textbf{ppp\,Q30:} Worn insulation at $X$ (live, after switch) touching the earthed
case $\Rightarrow$ L--E short through the fuse $\Rightarrow$ blows. Fault at $Y$ (neutral) does not.
